{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/14/codegen_prompts/7.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1692361792/14`\n- 题号：`7`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/14/7.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"7\">\n- `description`：网格中每个彩色环形轮廓内部的空洞形状被提取出来，作为\"印章\"盖在环形轮廓外部由同色引导线指向的目标位置上，印章颜色取自环形轮廓本身的颜色。\n- `Input structure`：背景为 azure。网格中有若干个由不同颜色绘制的单像素宽封闭环形轮廓（即中空的不规则连通环，内部有一个 azure 空洞区域，外部也是 azure）。每个环形轮廓外部连接着一条同色的单像素宽直线（水平或垂直），直线从环形轮廓的某个像素出发，延伸若干格后终止。直线末端的下一个像素位置（延伸方向上的紧邻空格）即为目标锚点。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个环形轮廓，提取其内部空洞的形状（即被轮廓完全包围的 azure 区域的像素坐标集合，相对于空洞的边界框左上角）。\n  - 找到该轮廓外部连接的同色引导线，确定引导线的方向和末端位置。\n  - 以引导线末端的下一格作为锚点（空洞形状的左上角对齐位置），用轮廓的颜色绘制空洞形状。\n  - 原始的环形轮廓和引导线保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：环的内部\"负空间\"才是信息载体——解题者需要发现输出图案的形状不是来自环本身，而是来自环围起来的空洞。引导线仅提供方向和距离的定位信息。这是一种\"反转图底关系\"的推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/dbff022c, train/df9fd884, train/5adee1b2, train/5623160b, train/465b7d93, eval/4c3d4a41, eval/581f7754, train/aa62e3f4\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3817\nmechanism=0.4517\nlexical=0.0127\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:sprite, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"df9fd884\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3141\nmechanism=0.3872\nlexical=0.0139\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, output:same_size, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/df9fd884.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/df9fd884.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the colored object from the lower bracket lane to the upper bracket lane and drop it to the bottom edge.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One frame color forms exactly two 4-connected bracket objects: a top-edge bracket open downward and a bottom-edge bracket open upward.\n- One other 4-connected foreground object sits in the lower bracket's interior column span.\n\nRule\n- Remove the movable object from its original cells.\n- Keep its shape and color unchanged.\n- Paste it with its bbox columns aligned to the top bracket's interior columns and with its bbox bottom aligned to the grid bottom.\n\nKey insight\n- The lower bracket identifies the object's source lane; the upper bracket provides the target lane, and the final vertical placement is bottom-aligned.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"monochromatic foreground object s whose bbox columns match the lower bracket interior\",\n  \"dst\": \"bottom-aligned slot d in the upper bracket interior column span\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.width == d.width; lower bracket gives the source lane and upper bracket gives d.columns\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear s; translate it unchanged into d with s.bbox.bottom aligned to the grid bottom\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5adee1b2\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3053\nmechanism=0.3744\nlexical=0.0134\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_component